PART 4 -- THE DIAGNOSTIC LADDER (post-verdict, every rung labeled)
  The registered thresholds treat the 8 properties as independent axes.
  They are not: log M_b and log v_flat are BTFR-collinear (rho ~ 0.94), and
  Q is itself an M/L-and-data-quality proxy.  These rungs decompose what the
  table means.  Canonical footing throughout.

  RUNG D1 -- the M/L-bounds census: where does the freedom pin?
  ups_best AT the 0.2 bound: 35, AT the 1.2 bound: 27, interior: 109 of 171 -- 62 galaxies (36%) are AT a bound: the freedom is REAL but many galaxies want more of it (population physics: old stellar populations push ups low)

  RUNG D2 -- the fixed-M/L baseline: did the freedom CREATE the mass
  structure in the offsets or INHERIT it from the fixed-M/L residuals?
  sd(delta) at fixed M/L=0.5: 0.1933 dex -> at ups_best: 0.1497 dex (the freedom absorbs 0.0436 dex of sd)
  the M/L-absorbed component (delta@0.5 - delta@best) has sd 0.0771 dex and correlates with log10(ups/0.5) at R^2 = 0.830 (the channel is what it claims to be)
  fixed M/L=0.5  : Mb+vflat plane R^2 = 0.936 (LOOCV 0.932, N = 152)
  at ups_best    : Mb+vflat plane R^2 = 0.814 (LOOCV 0.803, N = 152)
  READING: the mass structure is INHERITED from the fixed-M/L residuals (R^2 = 0.936 there, vs 0.814 after freedom); the freedom only shaves a near-uniform ~40% slice off the variance without changing the structure's identity

  RUNG D3 -- the registered-shape test: the theory's OWN self-similar
  mass geometry w = 2*log10(v_flat) - 0.75*log10(M_b) (coefficients fixed
  by the deep-asymptote arithmetic delta ~ 2 log Vf - 0.75 log Mb, ZERO
  fitted parameters), against the fitted plane, against the BTFR deviation
  R^2(delta_i, w_fixed)          = 0.284 (LOOCV 0.260)  <- kernel's own direction
  R^2(delta_i, plane, fitted)    = 0.814 (LOOCV 0.803)
  R^2(delta_i, geometry+dist 2ch) = 0.814 (LOOCV 0.803, FIXED directions)
  the fitted direction is cos = 0.984 from the theory's own in standardized
  space, but the BTFR degeneracy valley (sd(logMb) 0.92 dex vs sd(logVf) 0.28
  dex) makes R^2 along it steeply direction-dependent: the single-number R^2
  is NOT a shape verdict; the two-channel model with fixed directions
  reproduces the fully-fitted plane (same R^2, same residual)

  RUNG D4 -- the Q-gradient (measurement quality, the honest confounder)
  Q=1: n =  88   mean delta_i +0.0172 dex   sd 0.0908 dex
  Q=2: n =  55   mean delta_i -0.0415 dex   sd 0.1470 dex
  Q=3: n =   9   mean delta_i -0.3018 dex   sd 0.2601 dex
  the Q-gradient is monotone and large (Q=3 mean -0.30 dex, sd 0.26); a distance-error channel predicts sd ~ 0.18 dex for typical SPARC log-distance
  errors (0.12 dex) x the 1.5x amplification (delta ~ -1.5 delta_logD in the
  deep regime) -- the right order.  Q correlates with ups_best at R^2 = 0.103: low-quality galaxies also PIN at
  the M/L bounds (62/171 total at bounds), so Q and the bounds are entangled

  RUNG D5 -- residual aperture: what is LEFT after the best account?
  white-noise contribution to sd(delta_i): G036's within-galaxy 0.0447 dex
  over ~8.5 median deep points -> ~0.015 dex; the unexplained per-galaxy sd
  (best 3-prop model, LOOCV) is 0.0677 dex -- per-galaxy systematics, not
  white noise, and not any measured property

